]) ?></strong>.</li><li>Rent due date each month: day ____; first rent period: __________. The precise schedule, grace period, permitted payment channel, receipt process, and treatment of partial months must be completed in the signed lease.</li><li>Rent is not paid through this website preview. Pay only through a verified method named in the signed agreement and obtain a dated receipt.</li><li>Any late fee, returned-payment fee, or adjustment must be expressly written, lawful, and agreed before signing; no amount is created by this sample.</li></ul><h3>4. Advance rent and security deposit</h3><ul><li>Illustrative advance rent: one month = <strong><?= pesos((float)$unit['monthly_rent']) ?></strong>; confirm whether/when it is due and how it is applied.</li><li>Illustrative security deposit: two months = <strong><?= pesos((float)$unit['monthly_rent']*2) ?></strong>; the parties must confirm a lawful amount, receipt, custody, allowable deductions, accounting, and return timetable in writing.</li><li>Document every deposit deduction with its basis and supporting record. The deposit is not automatically the final month’s rent unless the signed agreement and applicable law permit this.</li></ul><h3>5. Utilities and other charges</h3><p>Water, electricity, internet, garbage, association dues, and any shared-area costs: list each applicable charge, meter or allocation method, billing period, due date, and dispute contact here: ____________________. The owner/manager should provide statements or meter readings. No utility charge is included unless expressly stated. Keep receipts and report suspected meter or billing errors promptly.</p><h3>6. Maintenance, repairs, and access</h3><ul><li>Tenant keeps the unit reasonably clean, uses fixtures normally, and promptly reports leaks, electrical faults, pests, damage, and safety issues.</li><li>Owner/manager arranges owner-responsibility repairs and coordinates non-emergency entry in advance. Emergency entry is limited to urgent protection of people or property; record the event and notify the tenant.</li><li>Tenant must not perform structural, electrical, plumbing, lock, or permanent fixture work without written approval. Responsibility for damage caused by negligence or misuse must be determined under the signed agreement and applicable law.</li></ul><h3>7. Building conduct, guests, pets, and amenities</h3><ul><li>Follow the published apartment guidelines, quiet hours, waste procedure, fire rules, and reasonable visitor/security check-in rules.</li><li>Guests may not become unlisted residents or disturb neighbors. Any overnight-guest limits must be written clearly in the signed agreement.</li><li>Pets: <?= (int)$apartment['pet_friendly'] ? 'the listing indicates pets may be considered; obtain written owner approval and the actual pet rules before moving in.' : 'the listing indicates no pets; do not bring an animal unless written owner approval is obtained.' ?></li><li>Parking, elevator, beach proximity, and PWD route descriptions are listing preferences only. Confirm assignment, access, dimensions, operating hours, fees, and unit-specific suitability; no amenity is guaranteed by this template.</li><li>No smoking, unlawful activity, hazardous storage, unauthorized alterations, or obstruction of exits/access routes.</li></ul><h3>8. Inspection, handover, and repairs inventory</h3><p>At move-in the parties should record date/time, meter readings, condition of floors/walls/windows/doors, supplied appliances, existing damage, keys/cards issued, parking stall (if any), and accessibility equipment (if any), with dated photographs. Each party retains the signed checklist. At move-out, agree a joint inspection and provide a written itemized account of any lawful deductions.</p><h3>9. Notice, renewal, early termination, and disputes</h3><p>Notice address and method: ____________________. Notice period: __________ days, subject to local law and the final agreement. Renewal request deadline: __________. Early termination, uninhabitable-condition process, default notices, cure period, deposit reconciliation, key return, and dispute-resolution venue must be reviewed by a qualified local lawyer and expressly completed. Nothing in this preview waives statutory rights or creates an automatic penalty.</p><h3>10. Written agreement and signatures</h3><p>Only a complete, dated, signed document and attached schedules approved by both parties set the final terms. Each party should receive a copy. Attach the house rules, inventory, utility method, parking assignment, accessibility disclosures, and any pet addendum where applicable.</p><div class="contract-signatures"><span>Lessor / authorized representative · signature / date</span><span>Tenant · signature / date</span></div><p class="policy-disclaimer">All amounts above are illustrative based on the current listing. No online payment or electronic signature occurs here. Have a Philippine-qualified lawyer review and complete this draft before use.</p></section></div>
<script>
(() => {
 const photos = <?= json_encode(array_map(fn($x) => ['src'=>$x['image_path'], 'caption'=>$x['caption'] ?: 'Unit feature'], $gallery), JSON_HEX_TAG|JSON_HEX_APOS|JSON_HEX_AMP|JSON_HEX_QUOT) ?>;
 const box=document.getElementById('unit-lightbox'), img=document.getElementById('lightbox-image'), cap=document.getElementById('lightbox-caption'); let index=0;
 function show(i){if(!photos.length)return;index=(i+photos.length)%photos.length;img.src=photos[index].src;img.alt=photos[index].caption;cap.textContent=photos[index].caption;box.classList.add('is-open');box.setAttribute('aria-hidden','false');document.body.classList.add('modal-lock')}
 function close(){box.classList.remove('is-open');box.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');document.body.classList.remove('modal-lock')}
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-gallery-open]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>show(Number(b.dataset.galleryOpen))));
 const galleryStrip=document.querySelector('.gallery-track');document.querySelectorAll('[data-scroll-gallery]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>galleryStrip?.scrollBy({left:Number(b.dataset.scrollGallery)*Math.max(300,galleryStrip.clientWidth*.65),behavior:'smooth'})));
 galleryStrip?.addEventListener('wheel',e=>{if(Math.abs(e.deltaY)>Math.abs(e.deltaX)){galleryStrip.scrollLeft+=e.deltaY;e.preventDefault()}},{passive:false});
 box.querySelectorAll('[data-gallery-close]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',close));box.querySelector('.gallery-prev').addEventListener('click',()=>show(index-1));box.querySelector('.gallery-next').addEventListener('click',()=>show(index+1));
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-modal-open]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const m=document.getElementById(b.dataset.modalOpen);m.classList.add('is-open');m.setAttribute('aria-hidden','false');document.body.classList.add('modal-lock')}));
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-modal-close]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const m=b.closest('.media-modal');m.classList.remove('is-open');m.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');document.body.classList.remove('modal-lock')}));
 document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Escape'){close();document.querySelectorAll('.media-modal.is-open').forEach(m=>{m.classList.remove('is-open');m.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true')});document.body.classList.remove('modal-lock')}else if(box.classList.contains('is-open')&&e.key==='ArrowRight')show(index+1);else if(box.classList.contains('is-open')&&e.key==='ArrowLeft')show(index-1)});
})();
</script>
